# ELECTRIC FIRE WITH SMOKE IN FLIGHT (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist booklet, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05, page 18 (owner decisions 2026-10-23, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28: the booklet is binding): the heading, every item, action, comment line and the boxed reference as printed; the booklet has no WARNING blocks here. The row marks are the numbers 1 to 8 as the booklet counts them. Rows 1 and 2 (the two ** rows, only with an oxygen system and above 10,000 ft) have no panel control and stay display lines, never graded. ECS - circulating air FRESH AIR is the state fresh of the circulating air lever; ECS shut-off PULL the state pulled; the Emergency front windows row is an optional step on the window; the Doors row is an optional step on the door release lever (the simulation has no landing, so the row below the comment line may be done at any time and is credited whenever the door opens); the printed comment lines (Continue, Land immediately, the emergency landing with its reference, Evacuate) have no panel action. All other text is own wording. The smoke source, the outcome threshold and hold time and the onset window are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-fire-flight
title: ELEC FIRE FLIGHT
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: "Page 18, ELECTRIC FIRE WITH SMOKE IN FLIGHT"
  verified: "2026-10-28"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cruise
briefing:
  situation: "You are in cruise flight when you smell burning plastic and smoke fills the cabin. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The smoke is getting thicker and its source seems to be electrical. The cabin air is set to recirculate."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.env_circ: recirc
  quantities:
    smoke_density: 40
parameters:
  smoke_source: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: ELECTRIC FIRE WITH SMOKE IN FLIGHT
procedure[15]:
  - kind: comment
    text: "If Oxygen System is installed and flight performed above 10,000ft:"
  - kind: line
    number: 1
    text: "** Oxygen System"
    action: "OFF"
  - kind: line
    number: 2
    text: "** Emergency Descent"
    action: "INITIATE"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Continue:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_av_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: av_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 3
        text: Avionic master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.av_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 4
        text: Electric master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_circ_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: circ_air_fresh
        severity: critical
        number: 5
        text: ECS - circulating air
        action: FRESH AIR
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.env_circ
          is: fresh
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ecs_pull
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ecs_pulled
        severity: critical
        number: 6
        text: ECS shut-off
        action: PULL
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.ecs_shutoff
          is: pulled
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: 7
        text: Emergency front windows
        action: OPEN as necessary
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: "Land immediately"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Consider and be prepared for:"
  - kind: comment
    text: "EMERGENCY LANDING (ENGINE OFF)"
    boxed: true
    action: "(page 9)"
  - kind: comment
    text: "After standstill and when engine stopped:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_doors
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: doors_open
        severity: optional
        number: 8
        text: Doors
        action: OPEN
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: "Evacuate"
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the cabin stays full of smoke; the density and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: cabin_smoke_full
    text: Cabin full of smoke
    hold_s: 30
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: smoke_density
      op: gte
      value: 95
# The smoke of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
# The smoke shows over the panel, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that it shows within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  cues[1]: cabin_smoke
